Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||09-16-2001||11:37 PM||||It's not the motor that made the car fast , it's the weight of the car. Geo is a light car , the 1.8DOHC is a pretty good little powerplant , but not enough torque to pull around a bulky 2500lbs ++ Fiero.<P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-16-2001||11:37 PM||||Any motor can be done... it won't be easy. You'll likely need the motor and tranny plus all the engine computer etc.... you'll also need to fabricate required mounts and probably a set of axles. You'll also need to figure out how to make the tranny shift and wire the PN switch....||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||09-16-2001||11:39 PM||||Hmmm...so you want more power? Why not go with a V8? Have you driven any V6 Fieros? They have much more power than the 2.5s. My first Fiero was an 86 2.5L 5spd. It wasn't that bad. I'd be ashamed to get beat by a metro. It's not fast by any means, but it had some take-off power.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">          <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
